{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<tools-used-before-summary>Bash, Grep, Read, Skill, ToolSearch, mcp__stdo_q05__contract_preflight, mcp__stdo_q05__dispatch_observe, mcp__stdo_q05__dispatch_start, mcp__stdo_q05__evidence_read, mcp__stdo_q05__return_capture, mcp__stdo_q05__return_check, mcp__stdo_q05__source_read, mcp__stdo_q05__tools_describe</tools-used-before-summary>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (Jim, acting as \"Root\"/operator) has me act as the actual installed-skill **Q05 Executive** for a tiny STDO fixture: correct `outputs/greeting.txt` from `Hello, Grace.\\n` to `Hello, Ada.\\n` (per R1/D1) through exactly one bounded Claude **Worker**, with a separately bound source-first Codex **Reviewer** that derives expectations before seeing the candidate. The Executive coordinates only: it must use the real `stdo_q05` MCP tools (`contract.preflight`, `dispatch.start`, `dispatch.observe`, `return.capture`, `return.check`, `source.read`, `evidence.read`) — never shell child launches, simulated returns, candidate mutation, publication, scratch files, or extra launches. Each phase is Root-selected via a STAGES.json SourceRef; I must acquire STAGES/PRIOR, preflight/dispatch/observe/capture/check, consume actual results and limitations, and stop with a compact structured handoff of exact refs for the next separately bound stage. The sequence so far: (0) initial stage-1 blocked by host permission denial; (1) reentry-1 corrected binding — Reviewer expectation succeeded, Worker failed login; (2) worker-auth-1 — preflight rejected (observation-array mismatch); (3) worker-auth-2 (current) — preflight admitted, Worker dispatched, Worker process ended returncode 1 with transport failure again even though the OAuth token passthrough is now present:true. Standing constraints (verbatim): \"Never inspect credential values or local config.\" \"No credential/config inspection, scratch, candidate repair or extra launch.\" \"If authentication or a required capability fails, stop and preserve the result with no workaround.\" \"do not repeat Reviewer or perform candidate review.\" \"Consume the actual Worker outcome and retain the existing actual expectation 9f6e54eb… for separately bound candidate review.\"\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - STDO 3.0.1-rc.1 method, a_c fd-support envelope `{schema:\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\", id, operation, arguments}`; SourceRef `{engine, root, path, object, sha256, selector}`; ArtifactRef `{id:\"sha256:…\", sha256}`.\n   - Executive/Worker/Reviewer role separation; closed-return `a_c.fd-support.closed-return/1`; return contracts; predicates (worker-result, expectation-recording, candidate-review); source-first independence; same-family limit (Worker/Executive anthropic-claude, Reviewer openai-codex).\n   - Native preflight mechanism `product-policy-preflight/1` in `a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support_core.py`; rule at lines 1866-1867: preflight `observations` must `_equal` `context[\"observations\"]` else `basis_stale`.\n   - `dispatch.start` takes only `{preflight}` (retry_of/reconciliation are ArtifactRef-typed; STAGES predecessor/reconciliation are factual SourceRefs, no retry receipt invented).\n   - Durable file event notifications in `control/evidence/notifications/<attempt>-N.json`; kinds reserved, supervisor_spawned, actor_launch_intent, actor_started, context_delivery, output_chunk, output_finalized, effect_observation. Waiting done via background bash `until grep … sleep 5` loop (no tight polling).\n   - Claude Code host launch flags: `--permission-prompts none` + `--allowedTools` must use underscore MCP tool names (`mcp__stdo_q05__contract_preflight`), not dotted.\n   - Evidence root `control/evidence/{objects,requests,notifications}`; physical capture `control/child-output/<role-dir>/{vendor.stdout,result.json,process.json,invocation.json}`.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `control/STAGES.json`, `control/roles/executive-TASK.md`, `workspace/TASK.md`, `workspace/TOOLING.md` — original mandate and tool binding.\n   - `workspace/specification/REQUIREMENT.md` — R1: greeting must be exactly `Hello, Ada.` + newline; R2: one bounded Worker, independent Reviewer, Executive consumes actual closed results.\n   - `workspace/design/DESIGN.md` D1; `workspace/inputs/name.txt` = `Ada\\n` (sha c4b7d453…); `workspace/outputs/greeting.txt` = `Hello, Grace.\\n` (sha dbfa3fcacaedf5e16d125ee1410774c6cb2d0bbd0a9fb07cacfe87fd362d29c7, unchanged throughout); `unrelated/sentinel.txt` sha 56686d9c…; target `Hello, Ada.\\n` sha 8b1560f395c0248eca4d2d6cc361825a9f8c00d11ce6f52b26eea2872573c2c1 (= CLAIM candidate_sources).\n   - `control/roles/CLAIM.json`, `PREDICATES.md`, `INDEPENDENCE.json`, `RETURN.md`, `worker-TASK.md`, `reviewer-TASK.md`, `worker-RETURN-CONTRACT.json` (3ab3f474…), `reviewer-RETURN-CONTRACT.json`.\n   - `control/plans/executive-actor-plan.json` — showed dotted `--allowedTools` defect; `q05/prepare_handoff.py:135` generates `'mcp__'+mcpname+'__'+op` (no `.`→`_` normalization).\n   - `control/actor-output/reentry-1/{STAGES.json, PRIOR.json, READINESS.json, HOST-NAME-BINDING.json, DOCUMENT-VALIDATION.json, roles/reviewer-TASK.md, roles/reviewer-RETURN-CONTRACT.json (7ee1c44a…), roles/INDEPENDENCE.json (8b409e86…)}`.\n   - `control/child-output/worker-reentry1/{vendor.stdout,result.json,process.json}` — showed `\"Not logged in · Please run /login\"`, is_error true.\n   - `control/actor-output/worker-auth-1/{STAGES.json (34f224cd…), PRIOR.json (1f2bce19…), roles/worker-TASK.md (9df0e5f4…, with \"Selected successor after authentication failure\" section), roles/worker-RETURN-CONTRACT.json (ac5c4dd8…), plans/worker-actor-plan.json (7241a78c…)}`.\n   - `control/actor-output/worker-auth-2/{STAGES.json (5b712a4b…), PRIOR.json (23273b74…), plans/executive-policy.json (30e2cd84…)}`.\n   - `a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support_core.py` lines 1861-1867:\n     ```python\n     observations = as_list(args[\"observations\"])\n     if not _equal(context[\"observations\"], observations):\n         guard(\"context observation currentness\", False, \"basis_stale\")\n     ```\n   - Evidence objects: contexts 46c496…/73d0ca… (reentry-1 worker/reviewer), e00fc354… (worker-auth Context: activation `urn:stdo-skills:T001:q05:claude:handoff:3:worker:activation:1:reentry1:worker-auth1` sha 0e6b040b…, frame qualification.q05.worker rev 3, subject_basis.observations = [sha256:99515157…] only); observations 8b1139e…, 45e33132…, 99515157… (stable, 23 entries), 43e58934… (target-preimage, greeting dbfa3f).\n   - Reviewer expectation artifact `sha256:9f6e54ebe544dcc4617512915684f55e85be7445a54cca6738aa98586dd0744f` (a_c.fd-support.expectation/1; claim 47bcca49…, candidate_population greeting.txt @ 8b1560f3…, source_first_observed true, 9 source_inputs, text deriving `\"Hello, Ada.\\n\"`).\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **Host permission denial (phase 0):** all `mcp__stdo_q05__*` calls auto-denied (\"no approval surface\"). Diagnosed dotted vs underscore allowlist mismatch; stopped without workaround; Root fixed names in reentry-1.\n   - **Worker login failure (reentry-1):** attempt sha256:89336016…, exit 1, stdout empty; host \"Not logged in\"; `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN` passthrough present:false. return.capture sha256:ef4a1211… (format_valid false), return.check evidence sha256:ac4e68cd… (consumable false, malformed_request). Reported; Root adjusted credential-name binding.\n   - **Preflight basis_stale (worker-auth-1):** preflight artifact sha256:7a4e861a… rejected; cause: STAGES gave 2 observations vs Context's 1 (ac_support_core.py:1866). Verified no file drift. Stopped; user confirmed \"Your prior hold correctly identified the operator-prepared observation-array mismatch.\" Root fixed STAGES to supply exactly Context.observations.\n   - **Worker transport failure again (worker-auth-2, current):** attempt sha256:2bf67976… exit 1, stdout 0 bytes, stderr \"Actor transport failed…\", despite token present:true. Cause NOT yet diagnosed.\n   - Minor: dispatch.start schema types `retry_of` as ArtifactRef (not nullable) → omitted it; reconciliation in STAGES is a SourceRef so not passed.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   Established the full actual-tool path (source.read → preflight → dispatch → observe → capture → check) and used file-based notification waits instead of polling. Reviewer source-only expectation phase is complete and retained (return sha256:d8594ce1…, check sha256:48799ef5… intentionally non-consumable pending expectation pin). Worker has now failed twice at host level; current open question is why the worker-auth-2 attempt failed with the token present (need child-output capture: vendor.stdout/result.json/process.json for the new attempt).\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Message 1: \"Exact control directory: …/claude-handoff-3/control. STAGES SourceRef {root control, sha256 7e099988…}. Use the installed STDO skill(s) to coordinate TASK.md as the Executive. Your exact stage1 mandate is control:roles/executive-TASK.md… Use the actual stdo_q05 MCP tools for your own preflight/dispatch/observe/capture/check, not shell child launches or simulated returns. Acquire the installed delegation skill/reference. Worker alone changes greeting; source-only Reviewer first retains its own expectations. Read each actual result and limits, then stop with a compact structured handoff for the selected next stage. This tiny fixture needs no whole-corpus research or scratch files.\"\n   - Message 2: \"Continue the same Q05 Executive session under the exact corrected binding. Prior factual record: …/control/actor-output/reentry-1/PRIOR.json. STAGES SourceRef {root phase, sha256 cf2f3ab6…}. Previous MCP calls were denied before server execution; no children existed. This successor normalizes only the observed exact MCP tool names and repairs the native IndependencePolicy shape. Use actual MCP operations… Acquire phase STAGES and the corrected policy/currentness; retain prior failures. The source-only Reviewer must produce its own expectation before candidate acquisition. Its current return is not a final candidate review. Consume actual results, then stop with exact refs/limitations for the next separately bound candidate-review stage. No config inspection, previous controls, scratch, candidate mutation or new launches beyond STAGES.\"\n   - Message 3: \"Continue the same actual Q05 Executive session. Root selected only the documented explicit local stdio MCP environment-name binding for the trusted stdo_q05 server. STAGES SourceRef {root worker_phase, sha256 34f224cd…}. The prior Claude Worker failed login before any candidate write; its native capture/check and your hold are retained. The actual source-first Reviewer expectation remains unchanged: {sha256:9f6e54eb…}. Acquire STAGES/PRIOR and current deciding inputs, then perform your own native preflight/dispatch/observe/capture/check for ONLY the same logical Claude Worker under this new activation. Use exact STAGES observations for preflight, but its original stable Context observation basis for return.check. No Reviewer launch or candidate review yet. Never inspect credential values or local config. If the documented binding refuses, retain failure and stop without workaround. Consume the actual Worker result with the retained expectation; return exact refs/disposition for a separately bound candidate-review phase. No candidate repair, publication, scratch, family/model change, or additional launches.\"\n   - Message 4 (current): \"Continue the same actual Q05 Executive. Your prior hold correctly identified the operator-prepared observation-array mismatch. This exact continuation is launched only after Root selection. Physical phase path …/control/actor-output/worker-auth-2. STAGES SourceRef {root auth_correction, path STAGES.json, sha256 5b712a4b2b927fdf7030c9bc89a11c9523d4cdef0e9c4329552b697b75d99917}. The exact unlaunched Worker Context, actor plan, task, grant identity, consumer and installed package remain unchanged. This successor policy adds the unchanged target SourceRef as grant.precondition, and STAGES now supplies exactly Context.observations for native preflight. The Worker original stable return basis excludes its intended output. Retain the previous rejection and initial failed-login attempt. The documented literal local MCP credential-name binding is unchanged. Perform your own preflight/dispatch/observe/capture/check for only this Worker; do not repeat Reviewer or perform candidate review. If authentication or a required capability fails, stop and preserve the result with no workaround. No credential/config inspection, scratch, candidate repair or extra launch. Consume the actual Worker outcome and retain the existing actual expectation 9f6e54eb… for separately bound candidate review.\"\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Complete the worker-auth-2 Worker cycle: `return.capture` for attempt sha256:2bf67976… (payload stdout sha256:c768159e445fd0aa9dde2543194312af0e012f8e4f8cd0254a065ae19a7b4c83, return_contract `{engine:\"workspace-regular-file\", root:\"worker_phase\", path:\"roles/worker-RETURN-CONTRACT.json\", object:null, sha256:\"ac5c4dd8260c53b75ba1d84676eda07bc5224df1e2b8303cbad5876cc35e954d\", selector:null}`), then `return.check` (return artifact from capture, context sha256:e00fc354…, consumer `urn:stdo-skills:T001:q05:claude:handoff:3:executive`, observations `[sha256:9951515725fc2ee89bad841a65f11aabc783b4b07dc701746be7c99f430027b2]`, predicates []).\n   - Acquire the Worker's raw/partial evidence from its child-output capture (find the worker-auth-2 attempt's dir under `control/child-output/`, read `vendor.stdout`, `result.json`, `process.json`) to state the actual failure cause — without inspecting credential values or config.\n   - Check the background waiter task `bgfqxm2ex` output (will be trivially complete since output_finalized already exists).\n   - Verify greeting/sentinel unchanged, then stop with a compact structured stage return: refs for STAGES (5b712a4b…, read evidence sha256:a97f7924…), PRIOR (23273b74…, read evidence sha256:6fe3f02e…), preflight (sha256:ff604ce3…, contract 578b80b9…, policy 30e2cd84…, admitted), dispatch evidence sha256:e745b07a…, attempt sha256:2bf67976…, observe evidence sha256:6a79e8a1…, process_end returncode 1, stdout/stderr refs, capture/check refs, retained prior failures (89336016… / ef4a1211… / ac4e68cd…; rejected preflight 7a4e861a…), retained expectation 9f6e54eb…, disposition stop/no workaround.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Immediately before this summary I had dispatched the Worker under auth_correction (`dispatch.start` → attempt `sha256:2bf679761388a7ca685a5b2898b4bc97c68709b31dbc827a74c0bd1c09c75cf5`) and run `dispatch.observe` after_event 0, which returned cursor 8 with the process already ended: `returncode 1`, stdout 0 bytes (`sha256:c768159e…`), stderr 96 bytes (`sha256:ac4cf732…`, \"Actor transport failed; acquire its raw/partial evidence before any separately authorized retry\"), `environment_passthrough [{\"name\":\"CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN\",\"present\":true}]`, supervisor policy `worker-auth-2/plans/executive-policy.json` sha 30e2cd84…, actor plan `worker-auth-1/plans/worker-actor-plan.json` sha 7241a78c…, effect_observation no changes/gaps. A background notification waiter (task id `bgfqxm2ex`) was also armed for this attempt. The Worker has not written anything; greeting.txt remains `Hello, Grace.\\n`.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Per the user's instruction \"Perform your own preflight/dispatch/observe/capture/check for only this Worker… If authentication or a required capability fails, stop and preserve the result with no workaround\": (a) read the worker-auth-2 child capture under `control/child-output/` (new worker dir) `vendor.stdout`, `result.json`, `process.jso